WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:06.080
When Elon Musk offered to buy Twitter for
$54.20 a share or $43 billion, he said he

00:00:06.080 --> 00:00:08.080
was:
“Not playing the back-and-forth game”

00:00:08.080 --> 00:00:09.760
He was moving “straight to the end”

00:00:09.760 --> 00:00:13.600
And this was his “best and final offer”
in the Securities and Exchange Commission

00:00:13.600 --> 00:00:14.240
filing.

00:00:14.240 --> 00:00:18.320
Twitter’s board tried to stop him in his
tracks by adopting a so-called “poison pill”

00:00:18.320 --> 00:00:20.400
to make it harder for Musk to buy the company.

00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:25.040
Under this structure, shareholders are allowed
to purchase newly offered shares at a discount,

00:00:25.040 --> 00:00:28.720
except for the person trying to acquire the
company, in this case, Musk.

00:00:28.720 --> 00:00:32.480
He’d have to purchase the new shares at
a higher price, so it’s a measure to stop

00:00:32.480 --> 00:00:36.000
him from taking over more shares of the platform
as soon as he hits 15%.

00:00:36.640 --> 00:00:37.760
He currently owns 9%.

00:00:38.640 --> 00:00:41.360
Musk is said to be fighting back with a plan
of his own.

00:00:41.360 --> 00:00:45.680
He is reportedly speaking with investors who
could partner with him in his bid for Twitter.

00:00:45.680 --> 00:00:49.760
One option according to the New York Post
is to team up with private equity firm Silver

00:00:49.760 --> 00:00:54.880
Lake’s Co-CEO Egon Durban, a Twitter board
member who led Musk’s effort to take Tesla

00:00:54.880 --> 00:00:55.520
private.

00:00:55.520 --> 00:01:00.400
The Tesla CEO is apparently also threatening
to appeal directly to shareholders.

00:01:00.400 --> 00:01:05.120
He sent out a cryptic tweet over the weekend,
“Love Me Tender” in reference to an Elvis

00:01:05.120 --> 00:01:06.320
Presley song.

00:01:06.320 --> 00:01:10.600
It could mean that he’ll bypass the board
and invite shareholders to sell - or “tender”

00:01:10.600 --> 00:01:13.840
- their stock to him at a premium so they’ll
make a lot of money.

00:01:13.840 --> 00:01:15.840
But what does he want with Twitter in any
case?

00:01:15.840 --> 00:01:19.600
I mean the guy already builds electric cars
and envisions trips to Mars.

00:01:19.600 --> 00:01:24.000
Given his professed mission to ‘save the
world’, it may actually make sense.

00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:28.240
If his goal is to save the world in one way
or another, he sees his purchase of Twitter

00:01:28.240 --> 00:01:30.080
as a way of saving democracy.

00:01:30.080 --> 00:01:34.560
He feels Twitter is not living up to its promise
of being a platform for free speech - which

00:01:34.560 --> 00:01:39.280
he calls “a societal imperative for a functioning
democracy” in the SEC filing.

00:01:39.280 --> 00:01:43.520
He said at a recent TED event that a good
way to tell if free speech exists is to ask

00:01:43.520 --> 00:01:47.520
this question: “Is someone you don’t like
allowed to say something you don’t like?”

00:01:48.080 --> 00:01:51.840
In the past few years, Twitter has started
fact-checking and suspending accounts.

00:01:51.840 --> 00:01:56.320
It most famously banned Donald Trump over
his tweets surrounding the 2021 Capitol riots.

00:01:56.320 --> 00:02:00.320
Musk’s patience with Twitter apparently
ran out when it suspended the account of news

00:02:00.320 --> 00:02:04.720
satire site The Babylon Bee which named U.S.
Assistant Secretary for Health Dr. Rachel

00:02:04.720 --> 00:02:09.200
Levine its “Man of the Year” after USA
Today named the transgender official one of

00:02:09.200 --> 00:02:10.800
its “Women of the Year”.

00:02:10.800 --> 00:02:14.640
Babylon Bee’s CEO Seth Dillon said Musk
reached out to confirm their account had in

00:02:14.640 --> 00:02:16.000
fact been suspended.

00:02:16.000 --> 00:02:19.600
Dillon said Musk “even mused on that call
that he might need to buy Twitter.”

00:02:19.600 --> 00:02:23.827
Purchasing his go-to social media platform
is certainly easier than starting his own

00:02:23.827 --> 00:02:26.480
social media platform which he said he has
seriously considered.

00:02:26.480 --> 00:02:29.520
So, what will Twitter look like under new
ownership?

00:02:29.520 --> 00:02:31.600
Will the former president be welcomed back?

00:02:31.600 --> 00:02:32.880
We’ll have to see.

00:02:32.880 --> 00:02:37.040
During the recent TED interview, Musk suggested
bans should be done with caution.

00:02:37.040 --> 00:02:40.000
And that timeouts are better than banning
people permanently.

00:02:40.000 --> 00:02:44.240
He suggested that when it comes to determining
if offensive tweets should be removed, the

00:02:44.240 --> 00:02:47.360
policy should always be to let the tweets
remain if there are any doubts.

00:02:47.360 --> 00:02:50.240
So when in doubt, leave it in, don’t take
it out.

00:02:50.240 --> 00:02:54.480
Musk has criticized Twitter’s secret algorithm
which it uses to decide what to show you on

00:02:54.480 --> 00:02:55.200
your feed.

00:02:55.200 --> 00:02:59.520
He said the algorithm should be open-sourced
so the public can inspect the underlying code

00:02:59.520 --> 00:03:03.087
behind the algorithm to ensure there's no
manipulation behind the scenes to promote

00:03:03.087 --> 00:03:03.200
some tweets over others.

00:03:03.200 --> 00:03:07.120
So basically, you’d know whether something
was done to promote or demote a tweet.

00:03:07.120 --> 00:03:11.520
He wants an edit button so people can revise
their comments and also wants to eliminate

00:03:11.520 --> 00:03:13.520
spambots and scam bots.

00:03:13.520 --> 00:03:16.400
Under his leadership, ads could be a thing
of the past.

00:03:16.400 --> 00:03:19.920
He has taken aim at Twitter’s revenue model
which relies on advertising.

00:03:19.920 --> 00:03:25.440
Not everyone is happy about an Elon Musk takeover,
including some Twitter employees and a Saudi

00:03:25.440 --> 00:03:27.360
prince and Twitter shareholder.

00:03:27.360 --> 00:03:31.520
Musk shot back by asking for the Saudi Arabian
kingdom’s views on free speech.

00:03:31.520 --> 00:03:34.800
The country is known to crack down on freedom
of expression.

00:03:34.800 --> 00:03:39.440
Others were reportedly already worried about
him joining the board, let alone buying Twitter.

00:03:39.440 --> 00:03:43.280
Musk abruptly canceled his plans to join the
company’s board which is made up of the

00:03:43.280 --> 00:03:48.640
current Twitter CEO Parag Agrawal, former
CEO and co-founder Jack Dorsey, and independent

00:03:48.640 --> 00:03:49.520
directors.

00:03:49.520 --> 00:03:53.760
In the SEC filing, he stated flatly: “I
don’t have confidence in management”

00:03:53.760 --> 00:03:58.240
A former SEC chair explained that joining
the Board could have limited his influence.

00:03:58.240 --> 00:04:00.080
Jay Clayton told CNBC:

00:04:00.080 --> 00:04:04.160
"When you go on the board of directors of
a company, your degrees of freedom as an investor

00:04:04.160 --> 00:04:05.680
are substantially restricted.”

00:04:05.680 --> 00:04:09.920
So instead of joining the board, he decided
he wanted to buy the whole shebang.

00:04:09.920 --> 00:04:13.200
Twitter has over 200 million&nbsp;
daily users - two-thirds&nbsp;

00:04:13.200 --> 00:04:15.120
of the size of the US population.

00:04:15.120 --> 00:04:17.760
Some of its users have been described as “woke”.

00:04:17.760 --> 00:04:20.160
An ideology Musk has blasted.

00:04:20.160 --> 00:04:22.400
In an interview with the Babylon Bee, he said:

00:04:22.400 --> 00:04:26.240
“Wokeness basically wants to make comedy
illegal which is not cool.

00:04:26.240 --> 00:04:28.960
Trying to shut down Chappelle, come on, man,
that’s crazy.”

00:04:28.960 --> 00:04:33.200
He’s referencing the attempt to cancel comedian
Dave Chapelle over transgender remarks in

00:04:33.200 --> 00:04:34.560
his Netflix special.

00:04:34.560 --> 00:04:38.960
He continued: “Do we want a humorless society
that is simply rife with condemnation and

00:04:38.960 --> 00:04:40.320
hate basically?

00:04:40.320 --> 00:04:44.400
At its heart, wokeness is divisive, exclusionary,
and hateful.

00:04:44.400 --> 00:04:49.600
It basically gives mean people a shield to
be mean and cruel, armored in false virtue.”

00:04:49.600 --> 00:04:53.920
But while Musk is presenting himself as the
king of free speech, others accuse him of

00:04:53.920 --> 00:04:54.880
hypocrisy.

00:04:54.880 --> 00:04:59.680
In February, Tesla employee John Bernal said
he was fired from his job after posting reviews

00:04:59.680 --> 00:05:04.240
critical of Tesla’s full self-driving software
on his YouTube channel, AI Addict.

00:05:04.240 --> 00:05:09.120
In 2018, a blogger who wrote not-so-flattering
articles about Tesla said Musk threatened

00:05:09.120 --> 00:05:11.280
to sue if he continued writing articles.

00:05:11.280 --> 00:05:15.680
His critics don’t see the richest man in
the world as the savior of free speech.

00:05:15.680 --> 00:05:18.000
By the way, how on earth will he pay for it?

00:05:18.000 --> 00:05:20.560
Most of his money is tied up in Tesla stock.

00:05:20.560 --> 00:05:24.880
Although he recently sold billions of dollars’
worth of shares he had to pay billions in

00:05:24.880 --> 00:05:25.600
taxes.

00:05:25.600 --> 00:05:27.520
And he gave billions to charity.

00:05:27.520 --> 00:05:32.080
Musk hired Morgan Stanley as an advisor for
the bid according to the regulatory filing.

00:05:32.080 --> 00:05:35.120
Banks are often brought on board to help with
debt financing.

00:05:35.120 --> 00:05:39.840
Having already become the rocket man, an electric
car entrepreneur, a builder of tunnels and

00:05:39.840 --> 00:05:44.480
brain-computer chips, he appears determined
to be a social media mogul as well.

00:05:44.480 --> 00:05:48.720
He already has the best and brightest engineers
at his disposal if Twitter needed more engineering

00:05:48.720 --> 00:05:49.440
